Finding: {"title":"TOCTOU race allows double-billing a checkride examiner fee (duplicate invoices)","severity":"HIGH","area":"Checkride fee billing idempotency","files":["src/server/routes/routes-checkrides.ts:2784-2854","src/server/routes/routes-checkrides.ts:2947-2982","src/server/routes/routes-checkrides.ts:3049-3082"],"detail":"All three billing-mutation endpoints (POST /bill, POST /student-signoff, POST /override-signoff) follow the same pattern: SELECT the checkrideHistory row, check `record.feeBilled` in application code, then later run createCheckrideInvoice() followed by an UPDATE that sets feeBilled=true. The UPDATE is not conditioned on `feeBilled = false` (no `WHERE feeBilled = false` guard, no transaction wrapping the check-then-act), and there is no unique DB constraint tying checkrideHistoryId to at most one invoice (confirmed via grep of schema/index.ts — no unique index on studentInvoices for checkrideHistoryId). Two concurrent requests (double-click, or a student sign-off racing an admin override) can both read feeBilled=false before either write lands.","impact":"Duplicate invoices/charges for the same checkride examiner fee, incorrectly reducing the student's account balance twice and creating a billing reconciliation problem.","recommendation":"Wrap the check-then-act in a single transaction with `UPDATE ... SET feeBilled=true WHERE id=$1 AND feeBilled=false RETURNING *` and only proceed to invoice creation if a row was returned (or create the invoice first inside the transaction and roll back on conflict). Alternatively add a partial unique index on studentInvoices(checkrideHistoryId) WHERE type='checkride_fee'.","confidence":"high"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.

